  <h2 class="mt-0">Right on Mapperley's doorstep</h2>
  <p>If you live around Mapperley Top, off Woodborough Road or along Mapperley Plains, Arnold is barely a detour. Lots of Mapperley owners head into the city for work, and dropping the dog in Arnold around 7:30am, then collecting them around 5pm, fits neatly around that commute.</p>
  <p>It's a short drive, and you're handing your dog to the same person every day: Vanessa, who has run Paws 2 Purrs from her home for 10 years and is licensed by Gedling Borough Council, the council that covers much of Mapperley.</p>

  <h2>The kind of walks Mapperley dogs love</h2>
  <p>Mapperley owners know the area is made for dogs. Up on Mapperley Plains the farmland opens out with long views, and Gedling Country Park, on the old colliery site off Spring Lane, is close by with its woodland and grassland paths. Woodthorpe Grange Park is just down the hill.</p>
  <p>Vanessa's pack spends its days in exactly that kind of place: woods, farm fields and water spots, with ball play on the way and most dogs off lead or on long lines. The exact routes change, and she'll tell you where your dog will go at your meet &amp; greet.</p>

  <h2>Which service suits Mapperley owners?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Working full days in town?</strong> <a href="/dog-daycare-arnold-nottingham/">Doggy daycare</a> means your dog isn't home alone. They're out with friends and come home tired.</li>
    <li><strong>Home at lunchtime some days, not others?</strong> A <a href="/dog-walking-arnold-nottingham/">walk with pick-up and drop-off</a> keeps their routine going.</li>
    <li><strong>Going away?</strong> <a href="/dog-boarding-arnold-nottingham/">Home boarding</a> keeps your dog in a real home, with sofa cuddles and daily walks, not a kennel.</li>
    <li><strong>A cat at home too?</strong> Vanessa does <a href="/cat-sitting-arnold-nottingham/">cat pop-ins</a> as well.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Big, bouncy or a bit nervous</h2>
  <p>There's no size limit, so Mapperley's huskies, Labradors and springers are all welcome. Huskies are Vanessa's favourites. Nervous dogs settle in too: one owner says her nervous dog was "running up the drive to be with his friends" within a couple of visits.</p>
